      <dc:creator>mermer</dc:creator>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div class="bbWrapper">Hi all,<br />
<br />
I have a new McCarty stoptail which I truly enjoy playing unplugged. It’s currently in D Standard / Drop C with 11-54 (I will put 56 for low E in the next setup). The only issue is the 58/15LT pickups; in my current setup they just do not work. For ambient, clean, melody type of playing they are good but for hard rock / metal riffage they sound too mid scooped, boomy in the lows, stuffy in the highs, worst of all worlds. Besides they cannot hold together under high gain. My main amp...<br />
